  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness based on the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes) is not reflected in the verbal report. The individual does not consider the distribution of probabilities across outcomes, nor does the individual mention or evaluate skewness. Instead, the individual focuses on the probability of experiencing a large loss (4000 euros) and compares that to the probability of a smaller loss (3000 euros). This reflects a risk-aversion or loss severity-based reasoning, not a skewness-based one. The decision reason requires evaluating which lottery has a greater portion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes — a comparison of the probability mass on negative outcomes. The individual does not make such a comparison. Furthermore, the individual's justification does not follow the rule of the decision reason (which prefers the more right-skewed lottery). Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning is conceptually different and does not align with the rule of skewness preference.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
